WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.933 --> 00:00:04.100
<b>Not every customer is tech-savvy</b>

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:10.100
<b>or willing to create an account for a health check or pay online for a service in advance.</b>

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.766
<b>Especially for people who want to do it spontaneously, this is often a major obstacle.</b>

4
00:00:14.766 --> 00:00:17.700
<b>That's why we introduced the InStore PrevCheck.</b>

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:24.566
<b>It allows you to serve a customer entirely at the pharmacy, from the questionnaire right through to payment.</b>

6
00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:32.366
<b>Customers can start the questionnaire by scanning a QR code at the pharmacy, for example on a poster or a display stand.</b>

7
00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:35.800
<b>Or you open your PrevCheck account,</b>

8
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>go to 'Measurements',</b>

9
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.166
<b>'PrevCheck InStore Questionnaire'.</b>

10
00:00:39.166 --> 00:00:43.700
<b>There you have two options for how the customer can fill out the questionnaire:</b>

11
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.100
<b>on the customer's own device,</b>

12
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:52.233
<b>When I click this, a warning appears reminding you that you'll need to charge for this PrevCheck later at your till.</b>

13
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:53.899
<b>Please don't forget that.</b>

14
00:00:53.899 --> 00:01:00.966
<b>As soon as I confirm the message, I see two options for sharing the questionnaire with the customer.</b>

15
00:01:00.966 --> 00:01:07.200
<b>The first option is a QR code that the customer can scan to go straight to the questionnaire.</b>

16
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:14.100
<b>And the second option is to send the questionnaire, or rather the link to it, to the customer by SMS.</b>

17
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.600
<b>You can use this option if the customer wants to come to you for the measurements at a later time.</b>

18
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:26.066
<b>Alternatively, if the customer doesn't have a device, for example, or can't fill out the questionnaire on their device,</b>

19
00:01:26.066 --> 00:01:32.333
<b>you can also make your pharmacy device available. To do this, click on 'On this device',</b>

20
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:36.133
<b>and the same message appears again, which I confirm.</b>

21
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:43.633
<b>Here you should also keep in mind that you're handing the customer your device, which may contain sensitive patient data.</b>

22
00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:47.700
<b>As soon as I confirm this, the questionnaire starts right away.</b>

23
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:54.499
<b>If you want to test the PrevCheck internally yourselves, click 'Internal use for training purposes' down here,</b>

24
00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:57.833
<b>so that the PrevCheck won't be billed.</b>

25
00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:06.699
<b>No matter which way the customer fills out the questionnaire, the six-digit booking code always appears at the end of it.</b>

26
00:02:06.699 --> 00:02:15.966
<b>You'll find all completed InStore questionnaires under Measurements, PrevCheck, and can conveniently select them there for the measurements.</b>

27
00:02:15.966 --> 00:02:19.466
<b>With the InStore PrevCheck, you charge the customer yourselves.</b>

28
00:02:19.466 --> 00:02:23.999
<b>That's the difference from the online path, where the customer pays in advance.</b>

29
00:02:23.999 --> 00:02:32.766
<b>One more small tip: to carry out the PrevCheck as efficiently as possible, we recommend starting the HbA1c or cholesterol measurement</b>

30
00:02:32.766 --> 00:02:36.433
<b>and then having the customer fill out the questionnaire.</b>

31
00:02:36.433 --> 00:02:43.233
<b>If you're now wondering how billing works, it's basically very simple.</b>

32
00:02:43.233 --> 00:02:49.266
<b>At the end of each month, we compare the number of PrevChecks done via the InStore path</b>

33
00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:52.666
<b>with those that came through our website.</b>

34
00:02:52.666 --> 00:02:57.366
<b>As a pharmacy, you always receive the same amount per PrevCheck.</b>

35
00:02:57.366 --> 00:03:04.800
<b>So there's no advantage or disadvantage for you, whichever path you prefer to serve your customers through.</b>
